==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} {{term|acertener|lang=fro}} ({{term|a-|lang=fro}} + {{term|certener|lang=fro}}).
See [[certain]].

{{etystub|explain better}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/æsəˈteɪn/}}, {{SAMPA|/{s@"teIn/}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|ăs-ər-tānʹ}}, {{IPA|/æsɚˈteɪn/}}, {{SAMPA|/{s@`"teIn/}}
* {{audio|en-us-ascertain.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|eɪn}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[find out]]; to [[discover]] or [[establish]].
#: ''As soon as we '''ascertain''' what the situation is, we can plan how to proceed.''

====Usage notes====
* '''Ascertain''' is a formal-sounding word. In informal contexts, it can sound [[pretentious]] and is best replaced with a more informal synonym.

